=== CONCLUSION ===
PCP exactly says: there exists Euler brick (a, b, c) such that
  d² + c² = g² where d = √(a²+b²) ∈ ℤ.
In our 18 Euler bricks up to 2000, this fails (miss > 0) in every case.

ℤ[i] viewpoint: this means d + ci ∈ ℤ[i] is NOT a Gaussian-square-times-integer.

